From: WendyOS maintainers <engineering@wendy.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: mark interrupted scan before synchronous disable

Backport the ordering fix from upstream 2cabe7ff1001b7a197009cf50ba71701f9cbd354.
The scan-disable completion runs before hci_scan_disable_sync returns. Set
HCI_LE_SCAN_INTERRUPTED first so it stops discovery instead of queuing an
advertising restart after the connection has already resumed the sets.

On the NVIDIA kernel this redundant restart attempts to reprogram enabled
extended advertising handle 0 and is rejected with Command Disallowed.

Also clear an unconsumed flag when disable fails or is skipped for suspend.
Return a disable error through advertising restoration without entering the
create-timeout cancellation branch: no create command has been sent here.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=2cabe7ff1001b7a197009cf50ba71701f9cbd354]
[Adapt to NVIDIA 6.8.12; clear the flag on unsuccessful/no-op disable and
return errors without entering the create-timeout cancellation branch.]

---
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -6466,8 +6466,12 @@
 	 * state.
 	 */
 	if (hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_SCAN)) {
-		hci_scan_disable_sync(hdev);
 		hci_dev_set_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_SCAN_INTERRUPTED);
+		err = hci_scan_disable_sync(hdev);
+		/* A failed or skipped disable has no completion to consume it. */
+		hci_dev_clear_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_SCAN_INTERRUPTED);
+		if (err)
+			goto resume_advertising;
 	}
 
 	/* Update random address, but set require_privacy to false so
@@ -6515,6 +6519,7 @@
 	if (err == -ETIMEDOUT)
 		hci_le_connect_cancel_sync(hdev, conn, 0x00);
 
+resume_advertising:
 	/* Re-enable advertising after the connection attempt is finished. */
 	hci_resume_advertising_sync(hdev);
 	return err;
